Description: Start polling for clients that claimed during driver open
 The SSC backend opens its sensors with a nested main loop.  A client
 (gnome-settings-daemon) that claims the accelerometer while that loop
 runs is recorded, but polling is only switched on for claims made after
 the driver is set up, so the orientation stays "undefined" and the
 light level 0 until the client claims again.  Once every driver is open,
 enable polling for each sensor type that already has clients.
Author: piano mainline contributors
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-09-29
---
diff -ruN isp-orig/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c iio-sensor-proxy-3.9/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
--- a/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
+++ b/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
@@ -781,6 +781,14 @@
 		DEVICE_FOR_TYPE(i) = sensor_device;
 	}
 
+	/* Opening a sensor can iterate the main loop (e.g. the synchronous SSC
+	 * calls), so clients may have claimed a sensor before its device was
+	 * open. Start those sensors now. */
+	for (i = 0; i < NUM_SENSOR_TYPES; i++) {
+		if (DEVICE_FOR_TYPE(i) && g_hash_table_size (data->clients[i]) > 0)
+			driver_set_polling (DEVICE_FOR_TYPE(i), TRUE);
+	}
+
 	if (!any_sensors_left (data))
 		goto bail;
 
